// Probe 65 — Cluster VI variant: closure capturing outer var + `??`
//
// Probe 45 used a closure that captured `h` (a struct) and called `??`
// on its field.  This probe captures a TEXT var directly and uses `??`
// on it inside the closure.  Captures interact with closure layout
// (the captured var lives in a synthetic closure-state struct), so the
// LHS of `??` is `captured_var` (Var → fast-path?).
//
// If 65 PASSES (because LHS is Var), the cluster-VI failure was due to
// the NON-Var LHS inside the closure body, NOT closure-ness itself.
// If 65 FAILS, closure synthesis breaks even the simple-Var fast-path.
//
// Pairing: 45 (closure with vec[i] LHS).
// Status: cluster VI border probe.

fn main() {
  s = "present";
  pick = fn() -> text { s ?? "fallback" };
  a = pick();
  assert(a == "present", "probe 65: got '{a}', want 'present'");
  println("probe 65 PASSED");
}
